# The breath gate: a phrase with no breath behind it is silent (a controller's stray notes at its
# threshold, breath CC 0); the level opens in a straight line up to Gate (the Breath page's K4, breath
# CC 2 by default), so the softest breath sounds, and above that the level is the breath's no more
wait 200
# no breath heard yet (a controller without it, or on another CC): notes play, as before
midi 90 3D 40
wait 200
expect amp 100
midi 80 3D 00
wait 300
# the breath heard once: a note with no breath is silent
breath 0 60 50
breath 60 0 50
wait 300
midi 90 3D 40
wait 200
expect gate 1
expect amp 0
peakreset
wait 100
expect peak_db_max -70
# breath CC 1, half of Gate 2: half open
midi B0 02 01
wait 100
expect amp >45
expect amp <55
# CC 2: open
midi B0 02 02
wait 100
expect amp 100
# more breath: the level stays (breath opens the filter, not the amp)
midi B0 02 7F
wait 100
expect amp 100
# tapering off with the note held: the level the phrase reached holds
midi B0 02 00
wait 100
expect amp 100
midi 80 3D 00
wait 300
# a stray note from silence again, breath at 0: closed
midi 90 3D 40
wait 100
expect amp 0
midi 80 3D 00
wait 300
# a stray note just after a phrase ends (breath and note off together, the stray 10 ms on): closed, not
# opened by the last phrase's breath still fading in the smoothing
midi B0 02 7F
midi 90 3D 40
wait 100
expect amp 100
midi B0 02 00
midi 80 3D 00
wait 10
midi 90 3E 40
wait 2
expect amp 0
wait 50
expect amp 0
midi 80 3E 00
wait 300
# the softest playing: a phrase that starts and stays at CC 3 sounds, at its full level (the old gate,
# open at CC 10 and squared, kept it under -50 dB)
midi B0 02 03
midi 90 3D 40
wait 200
expect amp 100
peakreset
wait 100
expect peak_db_min -45
midi 80 3D 00
midi B0 02 00
wait 300
# the release rings: breath and note off together, Release 360 ms, the level 40 ms on is the release's
tap ENV
expect title Breath
expect knob4 Gate
expect val4 2
wait 50
spin K3 300
wait 300
midi 90 3D 40
breath 0 100 30
wait 300
breath 100 0 20
midi 80 3D 00
wait 40
peakreset
wait 20
expect peak_db_min -42
# the curve doesn't move it: at Curve -100 (x^4), CC 2 is open
spin K1 -200
wait 300
expect par5 -100
midi 90 3D 40
midi B0 02 02
wait 100
expect amp 100
midi 80 3D 00
midi B0 02 00
wait 300
# Gate 10: wider, CC 5 is half open (the Gate shown is the breath CC it's fully open at)
spin K4 8
expect par70 10
expect val4 10
midi 90 3D 40
midi B0 02 05
wait 100
expect amp >45
expect amp <55
midi B0 02 0A
wait 100
expect amp 100
midi 80 3D 00
midi B0 02 00
wait 300
# Gate Off: a note with no breath plays, as with no breath heard
spin K4 -20
expect par70 0
expect val4 Off
midi 90 3D 40
wait 100
expect amp 100
midi 80 3D 00
wait 300
# the gate is the rig's, like the curve: the init sound keeps it
spin K4 3
expect par70 3
press SAVE
wait 1600
release SAVE
tap SAVE
wait 100
expect par7 60
expect par70 3
expect par5 -100
# kept through a restart, and a project saved before the gate was a setting (format 15) gets Gate 2
spin K4 4
expect par70 7
wait 5000
reboot
wait 200
expect par70 7
oldproject 15
reboot
wait 200
expect par70 2
expect par5 -100
# a panel key plays at full breath: never closed, with the breath heard (after the restart) and at 0,
# where Gate 2, from the old project, closes a MIDI note
breath 0 60 50
breath 60 0 50
wait 300
midi 90 3D 40
wait 100
expect amp 0
midi 80 3D 00
wait 300
# a panel key plays at full breath: never closed
key 4 down
wait 50
expect amp 100
expect level >5
key 4 up
wait 50
expect stale 0
